<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to auction two-year bonds of HUF 10 bln.</title>
<headline>Hungary to auction two-year bonds of HUF 10 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction 10 billion forints worth of the two-year government bonds of 1999/G series on July 17, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest period    23 June 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity		    24 July 1999</p>
<p>    Bills on offer			10,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price			    96.56 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum yield				  19.42</p>
<p>Average yield on two-year</p>
<p>     bonds at last auction (June 19)	 18.42 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.5 percent, payable semi-annually starting from January 24, 1998.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
